      "id": "f-lifetime-property-b9094b",
      "name": "FLifetimeProperty",
      "category": "CoreNet",
      "signature": "FLifetimeProperty(Rep Index, COND None, REPNOTIFY On Changed, False)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Rep Index",
          "type": ") :"
        },
        {
          "name": "COND None",
          "type": "Condition ("
        },
        {
          "name": "REPNOTIFY On Changed",
          "type": "RepNotifyCondition ("
        },
        {
          "name": "False",
          "type": "bIsPushBased ("
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "FLifetimeProperty\nThis class is used to track a property that is marked to be replicated for the lifetime of the actor channel.\nThis doesn't mean the property will necessarily always be replicated, it just means:\n\"check this property for replication for the life of the actor, and I don't want to think about it anymore\"\nA secondary condition can also be used to skip replication based on the condition results"
    },
